        "y0": 0.785344696969697,
        "x1": 0.870547385620915,
        "y1": 0.8293396464646464
      },
      "text": "Hence, until now, we showed that all edges in El can be monitored by the vertices of Man(Gk) \\ {vi",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.12941339869281043,
        "y0": 0.8031944444444444,
        "x1": 0.8705620915032679,
        "y1": 0.8551527777777778
      },
      "text": "l}. Hence, combining this fact with Claim 6.1 and 6.3, we can conclude that Man(Gk+1) forms an optimal MEG set of Gk+1. Hence, meg(G) = |Man(G)| for every strongly chordal graph G.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
